      "id": "leak-m14-observe-reports-read",
      "file": "src/Ashlar.Abstractions/Security/Egress/EgressSubject.cs",
      "old": "    public static void Observe(SecurityLabel label)\n    {\n        SecurityGuard.ThrowIfNull(label, nameof(label));\n        Frame.ObserveInto(Active.Value, label);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Starts a read scope for one read on this async flow, such as one tool call, and enters the read's frame: until\n    /// the scope ends, every decision on the flows inside it is made at <see cref=\"SecurityLabel.SystemHigh\"/>. When it\n    /// ends it observes what the read reported, or <see cref=\"SecurityLabel.SystemHigh\"/>, into every frame of the chain\n    /// it was begun on, and then, on the flow whose head it is, restores the frame it was begun in.\n    /// </summary>\n    /// <returns>The scope. Call <see cref=\"ReadScope.Complete\"/> when the read returns, and dispose it.</returns>\n    /// <remarks>Dispose the scope in a <c>using</c> block on the flow that began it, in order, as for\n    /// <see cref=\"Enter\"/>: a flow that never ends the read as its head stays inside the read's frame, at SystemHigh.\n    /// Work created and started inside the read keeps the read's frame, at SystemHigh, for its whole life.</remarks>\n    public static ReadScope BeginRead()\n    {\n        var chain = Active.Value;\n        var read = Frame.ForRead(chain);\n        Active.Value = read;\n        return new ReadScope(chain, read);\n    }",
      "new": "    public static void Observe(SecurityLabel label)\n    {\n        SecurityGuard.ThrowIfNull(label, nameof(label));\n        Frame.ObserveInto(Active.Value, label);\n        LatestRead.Value?.Report(label);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Starts a read scope for one read on this async flow, such as one tool call, and enters the read's frame: until\n    /// the scope ends, every decision on the flows inside it is made at <see cref=\"SecurityLabel.SystemHigh\"/>. When it\n    /// ends it observes what the read reported, or <see cref=\"SecurityLabel.SystemHigh\"/>, into every frame of the chain\n    /// it was begun on, and then, on the flow whose head it is, restores the frame it was begun in.\n    /// </summary>\n    /// <returns>The scope. Call <see cref=\"ReadScope.Complete\"/> when the read returns, and dispose it.</returns>\n    /// <remarks>Dispose the scope in a <c>using</c> block on the flow that began it, in order, as for\n    /// <see cref=\"Enter\"/>: a flow that never ends the read as its head stays inside the read's frame, at SystemHigh.\n    /// Work created and started inside the read keeps the read's frame, at SystemHigh, for its whole life.</remarks>\n    public static ReadScope BeginRead()\n    {\n        var chain = Active.Value;\n        var read = Frame.ForRead(chain);\n        Active.Value = read;\n        var scope = new ReadScope(chain, read);\n        LatestRead.Value = scope;\n        return scope;\n    }\n\n    private static readonly AsyncLocal<ReadScope?> LatestRead = new();",
